  "source": "NEET 2025",
  "question": "An electric dipole with dipole moment $5 \\times 10^{-6}$ C m is aligned with the direction of a uniform electric field of magnitude $4 \\times 10^5$ N/C. The dipole is then rotated through an angle of $60°$ with respect to the electric field. The change in the potential energy of the dipole is :",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$0.8$ J",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$1.0$ J",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$1.2$ J",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$1.5$ J",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "B",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "$U = -pE\\cos\\theta$, so\n$$\\Delta U = pE(\\cos 0° - \\cos 60°) = 5 \\times 10^{-6} \\times 4 \\times 10^5 \\times \\left(1 - \\frac{1}{2}\\right) = 2 \\times 0.5 = 1.0\\ \\text{J}$$",
